#!/usr/bin/env bash
set -euo pipefail
cat <<'HELP'
Return to the previous OS deployment

1. Run rpm-ostree status and find the booted and rollback deployments.
2. If a pending update is listed, cancel it first with:
       sudo rpm-ostree cleanup --pending
   Check rpm-ostree status again before continuing.
3. If a previous deployment is available, stage it with:
       sudo rpm-ostree rollback
4. Save your work, then reboot:
       systemctl reboot

If the desktop will not start, select the previous deployment from the boot menu.
Rollback does not restore your home directory, Flatpaks, or Homebrew packages.

Before testing an image, keep a working deployment with:
    sudo ostree admin pin booted

This command only prints instructions. It does not change the system.
HELP
